    <td colspan=3 bgcolor="#DEE7EF" class="catbg"><font class="catbg" size=2>Started by <a href="http://www.eq-eod.com/cgi-bin/yabb/YaBB.pl?action=viewprofile;username=dalathin" alt="View Profile: dalathin">Dalathin Drukane</a> | Last post by <a href="http://www.eq-eod.com/cgi-bin/yabb/YaBB.pl?action=viewprofile;username=dalathin" alt="View Profile: dalathin">Dalathin Drukane</a></font></td>
  </tr><tr height=80>
    <td colspan=3 bgcolor="#D8F8F8" valign=top><font size=2>Credit to Drakle for telling me about this, go to <a href="http://eqtoolbox.not.net/" target="_blank">http://eqtoolbox.not.net/</a> and register for an account (it's free), once your password is emailed to you, log into the site, and click on the 'Downloads' link.  Under the 'Other' Ui skins, you'll find a map-mod ui that allows you to tab through all the maps of all the zones in the game..It DOES NOT show you where you are on the map, but is VERY handy for those like me that get lost easily. <br> &nbsp;<br> Be forewarned its quite CPU intensive as all the maps are loaded so this isn't for those that are running on slow computers.  Install instructions are included in the zip file on how to install the ui mod. <br> &nbsp;<br> Enjoy! <br> &nbsp;<br> PS: For screenshots, go here: <a href="http://pub35.ezboard.com/fmonklybusiness43508frm16.showMessage?topicID=186.topic" target="_blank">http://pub35.ezboard.com/fmonklybusiness43508frm16.showMessage?topicID=1 86.topic</a> </font></td>
